// =====================================================================================
// 2x UI - Non-pixelated (AA) fonts   (sub-choice of the 2x UI component; runs AFTER the gate)
// =====================================================================================
// Swaps the portrait HP digits (NUMFONT) for an anti-aliased, TTF-rendered BAM (Roboto Condensed
// Bold), built by scripts/build_aa_font_bam.py into bam/bam_2x_ui/aa_fonts. Every glyph keeps the SAME
// per-glyph cell geometry (w/h/cx/cy) as the stock 2x NUMFONT -> identical layout/footprint. Digits are
// language-neutral, so it ships for every language.
//
// COLOUR MODEL (iwd2-re CVidFont::RealizePalette + CGameText SetColor(white,black)): the BAM palette
// is rebuilt by the engine as index1~=background .. index255~=foreground, index0=transparent. So the
// glyphs are encoded by INDEX (ink/body -> high index = foreground; AA edge + drop bevel -> low index).
// NUMFONT already de-doubles via its hd_match resref (IEex_UIScale_Patch.lua), so the AA BAM renders
// native-crisp at the 2x tier instead of being NN-doubled.
//
// TEXT FONTS STAY STOCK, ON PURPOSE. AA'd INFOFONT (parchment + worldmap labels) and AA'd floating
// world text (CGameText -> IEEXFLT) were both built, shipped and then DROPPED: the engine's text model
// is 1-bit ink over a colour-keyed background, so an AA face muddies the glyphs instead of smoothing
// them -- worst of all on the 1x world text. So:
//   · INFOFONT ships NO BAM here -> the engine loads the player's stock 1x font and NN-doubles it at
//     the 2x tier (sharp, and language-correct for free). Its de-double branch in
//     IEex_UIScale_Patch.lua MUST therefore stay >skip -- do NOT flip it to >hit.
//   · IEEXFLT (floating world text) stays the base component's COPY_EXISTING capture of that same
//     stock INFOFONT.
// Do not re-add an AA INFOFONT/IEEXFLT (any language) without reopening that call.
// =====================================================================================
PRINT ~[2x UI] Non-pixelated fonts: AA NUMFONT (portrait HP digits)~

// NUMFONT: always (language-neutral digits). Overwrites the stock silly_pixel NUMFONT.
COPY ~%mod_folder%/bam/bam_2x_ui/aa_fonts/NUMFONT.BAM~ ~override/NUMFONT.BAM~
